  "slides": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "title": "Re-evaluating Multimodal LLMs for Influenza Forecasting",
      "layout": "cover",
      "duration_seconds": 15,
      "speaker_notes": "My project re-evaluates multimodal LLMs for influenza forecasting. I examine MIFlu and compare twenty-eight implementations. The question is how model choice changes when average accuracy, peak errors, model size and statistical evidence are considered together.",
      "preparation_zh": "开场先说明研究问题：不是只复现一个分数，而是重新检查选模依据。标题中的 28 指整个比较名单，不表示四个维度都覆盖 28 个模型。副标题对应后面四条评价主线。",
      "follow_up_question": "What is the contribution beyond reproduction?",
      "follow_up_answer": "A four-axis re-evaluation with an explicit statistical correction and implementation/provenance limits. Broad negative-LLM findings already exist; this is the specific influenza audit, not a first-ever claim.",
      "sources": [
        "02_数字表格/BENCH_MSE_BY_MODEL_L.csv",
