      "figure": null
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "title": "Four evaluation axes ask different questions",
      "layout": "axes",
      "duration_seconds": 25,
      "speaker_notes": "I use four evaluation axes. Accuracy measures overall prediction error. Peak skill measures timing and height. Parameter efficiency compares model size with error. Statistical evidence asks what differences the test design can support. Their coverage differs: twenty-eight, twenty-eight, eleven and seventeen models. Those denominators must stay separate.",
      "preparation_zh": "请按四个问题解释，不要说成四个独立数据集。参数图只有 11 个有导出参数量的模型；配对检验只有 17 个非编码器模型。覆盖范围不同，是导师很可能追问的地方。",
      "follow_up_question": "Why do the denominators differ?",
      "follow_up_answer": "The source exports have different membership. Accuracy/peak cover 28 retained arms. Parameter data cover 11, excluding MIFlu and encoders. Paired comparisons cover 17 including MIFlu, excluding DLinear and encoders.",
