      "layout": "protocols",
      "duration_seconds": 25,
      "speaker_notes": "The historical reproduction uses ten seeds, while the wider benchmark uses three under shared cropped windows. Its twenty-eight implementations comprise thirteen conventional models, four LLM-based models and eleven frozen encoders. A new ten-seed expansion is underway. I keep its execution status separate from these historical results.",
      "preparation_zh": "本页两种协议均为历史结果。新的共同十种子扩展仍在进行，不能把新的执行计数当作已完成的公平比较。新 MIFlu 存储指标仍裁剪，其他 NPZ 用全窗口，需先统一评分。",
      "follow_up_question": "Why three seeds rather than ten for every model?",
      "follow_up_answer": "The retained benchmark is 28 × 4 × 3 = 336 cells. Three reflects the compute budget. More seeds can improve uncertainty; no adequate-power or no-benefit claim follows.",
